    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Finasteride 5 mg Q1x day alone or w doxazosin; ± meals."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Dutasteride 0.5 mg QD (w tamsulosin 0.4 mg QD in combo). Swallow whole: the capsule contents may irritate the oropharyngeal mucosa."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Finasteride lowers PSA by about 50% w.in six months. Set a new PSA baseline ± six months in and monitor periodically; any confirmed rise from the lowest value may signal prostate CA and should be evaluated, even w.in the norm range. An isolated PSA after six months or more: double it to compare w norm ranges."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "B4 starting, consider other urological conditions that cause similar Sx; prostate CA and BPH may coexist. Lrg residual urine vol or severely diminished flow: monitor carefully for obstructive uropathy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Finasteride tablets are coated, which prevents contact during norm handling unless they are broken or crushed; a preg woman who touches crushed or broken tablets should wash the area right away w soap and H2O. The same applies to leaking dutasteride capsules."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Finasteride:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉DI of clin importance identified. Dutasteride: caution w potent, chronic CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, ritonavir)."
     }
    ]
   }
